## 📊 Results Summary

| Component | Output |
|---|---|
| **Final Model** | Logistic Regression (SMOTE-balanced) |
| **Test AUC** | ≈ 0.61 |
| **Test F1** | ≈ 0.16 (expected; reflects class imbalance and dataset characteristics) |
| **SQL Insights** | 10 queries covering readmission rate, age risk, diagnosis association, admission source |
| **Streamlit App** | Deployed and publicly accessible |
| **Power BI Dashboard** | Interactive, stakeholder-ready |

The measured business value of this project is not the model F1 score in isolation. It is the combination of a stable, deployed predictive interface and a suite of SQL and BI deliverables that surface clinically actionable patterns from 100k patient encounters.

---

## 🔮 Future Improvements

- **Model explainability** — Integrate SHAP to surface per-prediction feature contributions; critical for clinical adoption
- **Feature engineering** — Consolidate sparse diagnosis codes into ICD chapter groupings; re-evaluate medication features as binary flags rather than counts
- **Advanced modelling** — Regularised Logistic Regression (ElasticNet), calibrated probability outputs via Platt scaling
- **Pipeline automation** — End-to-end sklearn `Pipeline` objects to prevent data leakage during cross-validation
- **Cloud deployment** — Containerise Streamlit app via Docker, deploy to AWS ECS or Azure App Service
- **Monitoring** — Add data drift detection for production model performance tracking
